# {{project.name}} agent application and document mapping

Read W `process/agent-instruction-policy.md` conditionally for the common contract on instruction interpretation, context/document loading, UTF-8/shell and completion reports. It is not a full read required before every task.

## Document mapping

| Kind of information | Source of Truth | Action on conflict |
| --- | --- | --- |
| The current user's work instruction | The explicit user instruction in the current session | If it changes the goal of an existing Issue, update the Issue body too before implementation |
| An Issue's goal, scope and acceptance criteria | The current body of that Issue | Do not change the scope through record entries or comments alone |
| Common agent hard guard | The marked block in `AGENTS.md` | Per-agent files or Skills cannot relax it |
| Work procedure | W skills and the W process documents the skills designate | If they conflict, do not implement; identify the conflicting documents |
| Module dependencies and edit boundaries | `{{bundle_path}}/project/module-boundaries.md` | Do not cross a boundary unless it is an approved architecture change |
| Current runtime behavior (as-is) | The checked revision of the declared `{{git.remote}}/{{git.base_branch}}` | If it differs from the business documents, treat the code as the observed as-is |
| Product rules after implementation is complete | `{{docs.business}}` | If the Issue's to-be changes them, synchronize them with the final code at the completion step |
| Basis of past decisions | `{{docs.reviews}}` | A historical record; it does not override current requirements |
| SDD working documents | `{{docs.sdd}}` | A temporary plan; it does not change Issue or business rules on its own |

